Binary ground truth would show values [0, 255] only. Values at 1-4 and
251-254 are JPEG ringing; a binarization threshold (>127) is required
and is recorded as a harness parameter. Midtones indicate genuinely soft
boundaries, where the threshold choice changes the ground truth.
Few distinct resolutions relative to file count indicates frames drawn
from a small number of source videos (see check 03).
